  "note": "Based on the official specification ORI-2-0027-OPR ver.2026-04-21. ID130 was checked on a real received frame (2026-09-13): the unit-quaternion norm, orbit radius and orbit velocity come out physically plausible. ID65/ID100 follow the specification but have not been checked against real frames yet. ID01 (MOBC HK) is not implemented: the specification's byte-offset table contradicts itself (byte 24 is defined twice, as 'RX microcontroller restart count' and 'power state of each device', and byte 22 is assigned to no item) and there is no real received frame to settle it. cw_frames (CW TLM) follows the fixed 28-byte format of ORI-2-0027e-OPR ver.1.1 (see document_cw). It was decoded by hand from a real CW reception on 2026-09-22 (callsign JS1YRU, two independent CW copies): the four UVC threshold bytes match the example voltages of Figure 3 (7.5 V / 7.2 V / 6.6 V / 6.2 V) exactly, and the satellite's internal UNIX time converts to the day of reception and advanced 73 s between the two copies (consistent with the 3 s beacon interval of Normal Mode), which confirms the offset assignment. The currents and angular velocities differed greatly between the two receptions (they are fluctuating quantities, so this is not a contradiction), so field-by-field plausibility has not been verified on real reception in the app yet. id_prefix=\"JS1YRUORIGAMI2\" was added because the order of Table 1 of the official CW specification ('call sign, satellite name, data section') reaches the CW decoder's block extractor (3 s threshold) as ONE block when there is no silence longer than 3 s between callsign and satellite name (seen on 2026-09-22 in fbsat59.log). See the 'OrigamiSat-2 frames' section of docs/telemetry.md.",
  "note_ja": "公式仕様書ORI-2-0027-OPR ver.2026-04-21に基づく。ID130は実受信フレーム(2026-09-13)で単位クォータニオンの大きさ・軌道半径・軌道速度が物理的に妥当な値になることを確認済み。ID65/ID100は仕様書通りだが実フレームでの検証はまだ。ID01(MOBC HK)は仕様書のbyteオフセット表に矛盾(byte24が「RXマイコン再起動回数」と「各機器電源状態」で二重定義され、byte22がどの項目にも割り当てられていない)があり、実受信フレームでの裏付けが取れるまで未実装。cw_frames(CW TLM)はORI-2-0027e-OPR ver.1.1(document_cw参照)の28バイト固定フォーマットに基づく。2026-09-22のCW実受信(コールサインJS1YRU、独立した2回のCWコピー)で手動デコードし、UVC閾値4バイトがFigure 3の例示電圧値(7.5V/7.2V/6.6V/6.2V)と完全一致・衛星内部UNIX時刻が受信当日の日付に変換され2回の受信間で73秒進んでいた(Normal Modeの3秒間隔ビーコンと矛盾しない)ことから、オフセット割り当ての正しさを確認済み。電流・角速度は2回の受信で値が大きく食い違った(値そのものが変動する項目であるため無矛盾)ため、アプリでの実受信によるフィールド単位の妥当性検証はまだ行っていない。id_prefix=\"JS1YRUORIGAMI2\"は、公式CW仕様書Table1の「call sign, satellite name, data section」の送信順を、コールサイン・衛星名の間に3秒を超える無音が無いままCWデコーダーのブロック抽出器(3秒閾値)へ渡すと1個のブロックに繋がってしまう実挙動(2026-09-22、fbsat59.logで確認)に合わせて追加した。詳細はdocs/telemetry.mdの「OrigamiSat-2のフレーム」節参照。",
